{
  "id": "11",
  "title": "Memory Management",
  "content": "<div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.12) 0%, rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.04) 100%); border: 1px solid rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.2); border-left: 4px solid #2DD4BF; padding: 32px; margin-bottom: 60px; border-radius: 4px; position: relative; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"position: absolute; top: -20px; right: -20px; opacity: 0.05; transform: rotate(15deg);\"><svg width=\"120\" height=\"120\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2DD4BF\" stroke-width=\"1\"><path d=\"M21 16V8a2 2 0 0 0-1-1.73l-7-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 0l-7 4A2 2 0 0 0 3 8v8a2 2 0 0 0 1 1.73l7 4a2 2 0 0 0 2 0l7-4A2 2 0 0 0 21 16z\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"4\"/></svg></div><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-heading); font-weight: 300;\">Photon implements a <strong>Zero-Churn</strong> memory strategy. By utilizing high-frequency object pooling and atomic resets, we eliminate the GC pressure that typically degrades high-traffic Node.js applications.</p></div><h2>The Allocation Vacuum</h2><p>In traditional frameworks, every request is a memory event. In Photon, a request is a <strong>Memory Pipeline</strong>. We pre-allocate the infrastructure so your logic runs on silicon, not on the heap garbage collector.</p><div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; margin: 48px 0;\" class=\"bento-grid\"><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(45,212,191,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"> <div style=\"color: #2DD4BF; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M21 12A9 9 0 1 1 12 3v9z\"/><path d=\"M21 12c-3 0-6 3-6 6\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">OBJECT_POOLING</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Context objects are recycled immediately after response delivery, reducing allocations by over 99.6% at 10k RPS.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(45,212,191,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"><div style=\"color: #2DD4BF; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 2v4\"/><path d=\"m16.2 7.8 2.9-2.9\"/><path d=\"M18 12h4\"/><path d=\"m16.2 16.2 2.9 2.9\"/><path d=\"M12 18v4\"/><path d=\"m4.9 19.1 2.9-2.9\"/><path d=\"M2 12h4\"/><path d=\"m4.9 4.9 2.9 2.9\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">LAZY_HYDRATION</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Headers and body data are only parsed when accessed. If your handler doesn't touch it, it never exists on the heap.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(45,212,191,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"><div style=\"color: #2DD4BF; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M3 2v7c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h4\"/><path d=\"M3 2h20\"/><path d=\"M21 2v7c0 1.1-.9 2-2 2h-4\"/><path d=\"M9 11v11\"/><path d=\"M15 11v11\"/><path d=\"M9 11h6\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">DEEP_CLEANSE</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">A strict reset protocol ensures that user data references are scrubbed before an object returns to the pool, preventing memory leaks.</p></div></div><h2>Allocation Elimination Matrix</h2><p>Our benchmarks show a dramatic reduction in heap fragmentation compared to traditional request-per-object frameworks.</p><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; margin: 40px 0; border-radius: 4px;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 24px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; color: #2DD4BF; margin-bottom: 12px; font-family: var(--font-technical);\"><span>PHOTON_POOLED_ALLOCATIONS</span> <span>~1 / 256 REQ</span></div><div style=\"height: 8px; background: rgba(45,212,191,0.1); width: 100%; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"height: 100%; width: 2%; background: #2DD4BF; box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(45,212,191,0.5);\"></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 0;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; color: #6B7280; margin-bottom: 12px; font-family: var(--font-technical);\"><span>TRADITIONAL_ALLOCATIONS</span> <span>1 / 1 REQ</span></div><div style=\"height: 8px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); width: 100%; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"height: 100%; width: 100%; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.2);\"></div></div></div><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; font-family: var(--font-technical); border: none; padding: 0;\">// METRIC: 99.6% REDUCTION IN V8 GARBAGE COLLECTION FREQUENCY</p></div><h2>The Recycle Lifecycle</h2><p>Context objects follow a deterministic path through the engine pipeline.</p><pre><code>// Internal Context Lifecycle\n1. acquire()  // Retreive from Fast-Pool\n2. rehydrate()// Inject new Request headers/params\n3. execute()  // Run Middleware + Business Logic\n4. scramble() // Atomic reference clearing\n5. release()  // Return to pool for next request</code></pre><div style=\"background: rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.05); border: 1px solid rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.1); border-left: 4px solid #2DD4BF; padding: 24px; margin: 40px 0; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;\"><h4 style=\"margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 900; color: #2DD4BF; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em;\">// DEV_PROTOCOL: REFERENCE_HYGIENE</h4><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 15px; font-style: italic; color: var(--text-heading); opacity: 0.9; border: none; padding: 0;\">Because contexts are pooled, never hold a reference to <code>c</code> outside the scope of the request (e.g., inside a long-running <code>setTimeout</code>). Doing so will access a context that has already been scrubbed or reassigned to a new request.</p></div><div style=\"background: linear-gradient(to right, rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.1), transparent); border-left: 4px solid #6366F1; padding: 24px; margin-top: 60px; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500; font-style: italic; border: none; padding: 0; color: var(--text-heading);\"><strong>Architect's Note:</strong> Photon's memory strategy is \"Self-Healing.\" Under massive traffic spikes, the pool expands dynamically. As traffic subsides, the overflow handles are naturally purged, returning the application to its base idling footprint.</p></div>",
